# Provenance of the byte-exact upstream base/install.yaml; deployment is offline.
# Compatibility: https://gateway.envoyproxy.io/news/releases/matrix/
# v1.9 supports Kubernetes 1.33-1.36, Gateway API v1.6.1 and Envoy v1.39.x.
# Upstream certgen behavior and generated Secret names:
# https://github.com/envoyproxy/gateway/blob/v1.9.2/internal/cmd/certgen.go
# https://github.com/envoyproxy/gateway/blob/v1.9.2/internal/provider/kubernetes/secrets.go
# Local patches keep controller/certgen/shutdown-manager images digest-pinned,
# remove unused rate-limit config, bound and retain certgen, and roll the
# controller when its fixed-name ConfigMap changes. Upstream selectors stay intact.
# Apply order: platform namespaces -> crds -> prerequisites -> certgen -> controller.
# Certgen needs the prerequisites webhook and writes its caBundle. Never commit
# generated Secret values or add caBundle to the declared webhook configuration.
# Reusing a completed Job requires checking its desired spec and generated Secrets.
# A partial pre-existing Secret set must fail: certgen otherwise mixes old/new CAs.
VERSION=v1.9.2
SOURCE_URL=https://github.com/envoyproxy/gateway/releases/download/v1.9.2/install.yaml
SHA256=0412a72907e57ff9b73c56a7bf6df5190bf0f6e4f8bb4bba34e38630bbab5778
